@startuml

salt
{
  <b>AUTHOR A CONVENTION FOR A KIND</b>  { Kind | Terms | Review | Saved | History }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>1. Choose the kind</b>
      --
      Party ACCOUS. 26 kinds, one table each; the kind decides which fields are drawn.
      --
      {#
        Kind | Term columns | Party holds | The act asks for
        deposit | 8 | 163 | calendar, convention, day count, settlement days
        <b>swap</b> | 7 | <b>320</b> | fixed leg schedule and a floating index
        tenor_basis_swap | 7 | 37 | two legs
        ... 23 more kinds ...
      }
      <i>The filter takes id_one_of only, so "these terms are not here yet" is a page of rows read in words.</i>
      [ Continue ]
    } | {
      <b>2. Author its terms</b>  -  swap, party ACCOUS
      --
      {#
        Field | Value | Source
        Key | ^AED-EIBOR-6M-SWAP      ^ | authored here; the run refers to the document by it
        Fixed Calendar | ^AED^v | from calendar_names
        Fixed Frequency | ^Annual^v | from payment_frequencies
        Fixed Convention | ^ModifiedFollowing^v | from business_day_convention_types
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | ^ACT/365^v | from day_count_fraction_types
        Index | ^AED-EIBOR-6M^v | from floating_index_types
        Float Frequency | ^Semi-Annual^v | from payment_frequencies
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | (empty)v | from sub_periods_coupon_types
      }
      <i>Empty and stated are different claims: an empty column is drawn empty and not defaulted.</i>
      <i>The grouping is the screen's: the table carries no leg object.</i>
      [ Read calendars... ] | [ Back ] | [ Review ]
    }
  }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>3. Review</b>
      --
      7 fields filled, 1 left empty.
      {#
        Field | Value
        Fixed leg |
        Fixed Calendar | AED
        Fixed Frequency | Annual
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | ACT/365
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | (empty)
      }
      <i>None of the 320 existing swap documents states this term set.</i>
      [ Back ] | [ Save as a new document ]
    } | {
      <b>4. Saved</b>
      --
      <b>AED-EIBOR-6M-SWAP is saved as version 1</b>
      by m.okafor at 2026-10-18 10:12, reason system.new_record
      precondition: must_not_exist (a key already present is refused, never overwritten)
      --
      <b>What the write did not do</b>
      It did not mark this document as the one a run takes: no such mark exists.
      It did not attach it to a report: a conventions configuration holds no rows.
      It added a document every run of ACCOUS will now carry, beside the 320 others.
      [ See the history ] | [ Back to the kind ] | [ Another kind ]
      --
      <b>5. History</b>  version: { <b>v1</b> }
      {#
        Envelope | Value
        version | 1
        valid_from | 2026-10-18 10:12
        valid_to | (open)
        modified_by | m.okafor
        change_reason_code | system.new_record
        change_commentary | authored for the AED 6M swap the curated set does not state
      }
      <i>A later correction closes this row with valid_to and writes version 2 with valid_from.</i>
    }
  }
}

@enduml
